From 28c7630f5a770be55235708f6551de69c13a020b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: os-patcher <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Feb 2026 15:26:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] security note: CVE-2026-24882 not applicable to gnupg2 2.2.x

---
 ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md | 56 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 56 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md

diff --git a/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ef91b6e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ROOT-SECURITY-RELEASE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# Why CVE-2026-24882 Does Not Affect gnupg2 in Debian Bookworm
+
+## Overview
+
+Debian Bookworm ships **gnupg2** version **2.2.40** (2.2.x branch). This note documents why **CVE-2026-24882** does not apply to this package and no code patch is required.
+
+***
+
+## What Is CVE-2026-24882?
+
+CVE-2026-24882 is a **stack-based buffer overflow** in GnuPG's **TPM2 handling code** (the **tpm2da** component). It can be triggered during CMS (S/MIME) EnvelopedData message handling when TPM2 is involved. Affected upstream versions are **2.5.13 through 2.5.16**; the fix is in **GnuPG 2.5.17**.
+
+***
+
+# CVE Breakdown
+
+***
+
+## CVE-2026-24882 – TPM2 Buffer Overflow (Not Applicable to 2.2.x)
+
+- **Component:** GnuPG **tpm2da** (TPM2 handling)
+- **Issue:** Stack-based buffer overflow in TPM2 decryption code
+- **Impact:** DoS or potential remote code execution when processing crafted input
+- **Upstream affected:** GnuPG **2.5.13–2.5.16** (fixed in 2.5.17)
+
+### Why Bookworm gnupg2 (2.2.40) Is Not Affected
+
+| Check | Result |
+|-------|--------|
+| **Version branch** | Bookworm ships **2.2.40** (2.2.x). The CVE affects **2.5.13–2.5.16** (2.5.x) only. |
+| **Vulnerable code** | TPM2 support (tpm2daemon/tpm2da) was introduced in **GnuPG 2.3**. The **2.2.x series does not contain any TPM2 handling code**. |
+| **Package contents** | No TPM2-related code or patches exist in the Debian Bookworm gnupg2 source; the vulnerable code path cannot be executed. |
+
+### Conclusion
+
+- **CVE-2026-24882 does not affect** the gnupg2 package in Debian Bookworm.
+- The **vulnerable component (TPM2 handling) is not present** in the 2.2.x branch.
+- **No patch is required** for this CVE on Bookworm's gnupg2; this folder exists only to document the assessment so the note is included as part of the application.
+
+***
+
+## Summary
+
+- CVE-2026-24882 is a real vulnerability in GnuPG **2.5.x** (TPM2 code).
+- Debian Bookworm gnupg2 is **2.2.40** (2.2.x), which has **no TPM2 code**.
+- Scanners may still flag the CVE by version comparison; this document explains why the package is **not actually affected**.
+
+**Best practice:** Keep base images and packages up to date; for CVE-2026-24882 specifically, no action is needed on Bookworm's gnupg2.
+
+***
+
+## References
+
+- [GnuPG Security Advisory (T8044)](https://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnupg-announce/2026q1/000501.html)
+- [Debian security tracker – gnupg2](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/source-package/gnupg2)
+- [NVD CVE-2026-24882](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-24882)
-- 
